                <pb facs="0333" n="199" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg199"/>

                <head>No. 142.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Denby.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-09-05"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 5,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 227.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 422 of July 29,
                    1887, concerning.-the reduction of the likin tax on kerosene oil at Canton from
                    $1.30 to 50 cents per case.</p>
                <p>The Department is equally pleased as yourself at this very considerable
                    reduction, and shares also in the gratitude which you express in behalf of the
                    labors of Mr. Seymour, consul at that port, by whose instrumentality this
                    reduction was largely effected.</p>
                <p>You will convey to Mr. Seymour a suitable expression of the Department’s
                    thanks.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F.
                        Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
